  "outcome": "completed",
  "summary": "Made local drop terminal across ordinary and authored anchors without poisoning projection-hidden targets; reduced annotations to resolve-only borrowed targets, explicit typed reader stores and separately owned headless disposal; removed the generic provider and public diagnostics; moved comment mode to two exact mounted views over one model; kept Decoration as the paint owner; and retained the existing private node-key mapping kernel after all matched candidates failed the frozen promotion gate.",
  "proof": {
    "state": "verified",
    "evidence": [
      {
        "path": "docs/plans/artifacts/annotations-architecture-adoption/verification.json",
        "sha256": "d0036870c732c80de368240625da09e9494bdc3d72d0b4060d9a1bd1e9c8bcd6",
        "claim": "Records passing focused anchor, annotation, Comments and browser contracts; strict Plite package/tooling/full-Chromium closure; complete website/docs/registry/type closure; and generated-owner checks."
      },
      {
        "path": "docs/plans/artifacts/annotations-architecture-adoption/annotation-view-index-benchmark.json",
        "sha256": "a5f377577997c77e62e013efb3df83c5628f3165005ed366457a879ff3db4eb6",
        "claim": "Records matched 1/2/4-view and 1k/10k/100k dense/distributed cohorts with zero correctness failures, stable source, no candidate promotion and the current baseline retained."
      }
    ],
    "limits": "Verified current-source local behavior and performance plus Chromium browser behavior. Firefox/WebKit, physical devices, production deployment and replicated terminal absence across peers were not exercised. The benchmark rejects the tested private replacements under the frozen local gate; it does not claim superiority over every possible external index."
  },
